{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/evals/no-qual-files/graders/no-skill-fired.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:06:38.814612Z","id":"251904038e9e3751ce1715023839206a26b69b043cd8809b6143cbea3d19efae","body":{"detail":"The grader's input_match is '\"skill\"\\s*:\\s*\"qual:' (plugins/claude-code/evals/no-qual-files/graders/no-skill-fired.md), which only matches when the Skill tool's JSON input carries the 'qual:' prefix. Every positive skill-fired grader in this same suite matches the looser '\"skill\"\\s*:\\s*\"(?:qual:)?<name>\"' instead (e.g. plugins/claude-code/evals/design-rejects-option/graders/skill-fired.md, plugins/claude-code/evals/triage-open/graders/skill-fired.md), i.e. they treat a bare, unprefixed skill name as an equally valid firing signal. That leniency exists because Claude Code resolves unqualified Skill dispatch whenever the name is unambiguous, which is the normal case for a single-plugin eval run (no other plugin is loaded to create a naming collision). So a qual skill (e.g. recording-design-decisions) that fires bare, without the 'qual:' prefix, during the no-qual-files run is not matched by this grader; min:0/max:0 still sees 0 matches and the case passes even though the exact thing it exists to catch -- a qual skill firing when there are no .qual files -- happened.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"07e433d8a653f8acae8048bf2d96782bc23e1f3678ca701174495ecc64ad1296"},"suggested_fix":"Broaden the regex to also match the bare form, mirroring the (?:qual:)? pattern already used by every skill-fired.md grader in this suite, e.g. '\"skill\"\\s*:\\s*\"(?:qual:)?(using-qualifier|recording-design-decisions|planning-from-threads|consulting-threads|closing-the-loop|reviewing-into-qualifier|triaging-threads|escalating-decisions|handing-off-threads)\"'.","summary":"no-skill-fired grader misses bare (unprefixed) Skill invocations, letting a qual skill fire undetected in the no-qual-files case","tags":["review","review:claude-plugin-pr14","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/evals/no-qual-files/graders/no-skill-fired.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:17:14.838900Z","id":"e75ae89fe5c594e0b260d6747c872a8a89a48fec0efc465eab2da426e0e43ffe","body":{"detail":"plugins/claude-code/evals/no-qual-files/graders/no-skill-fired.md:4 is input_match '\"skill\"\\s*:\\s*\"qual:' with min:0/max:0, and it is the only grader in that case (graders/ holds just this file). The positive graders accept the bare form, e.g. plugins/claude-code/evals/design-rejects-option/graders/skill-fired.md:4 '(?:qual:)?recording-design-decisions'. The Claude Code plugin-evals docs (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugin-evals.md, 'Check that a skill fired') recommend '\"skill\"\\s*:\\s*\"(?:[\\w-]+:)?your-skill-name\"' and say this 'passes when Claude invoked that skill ... including by its namespaced plugin-name:skill-name form', so a bare name is an expected form of the Skill input. Why it is not a blocker: this is a gap in the eval's coverage. Plugin behavior for users does not change. A false pass hides a regression but ships no defect, so the fix can land after merge.","kind":"comment","references":"251904038e9e3751ce1715023839206a26b69b043cd8809b6143cbea3d19efae","summary":"confirmed (not a blocker): the grader only matches the qual:-prefixed form, so a bare-name Skill call would pass unnoticed","tags":["verified","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/claude-code/evals/no-qual-files/graders/no-skill-fired.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T17:00:14.409063Z","id":"7057a17693a1f2ec5bdc9471604922c9629e09953d870c6d4df16655e967383b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6a733e989f42ba0d270a61225768f5959841d00f","summary":"input_match is now '\"skill\"\\s*:\\s*\"(?:qual:)?(...)\"' (no-skill-fired.md:4), matching the bare skill name as well as the qual:-prefixed form: scripts/test-plugin.sh ok: eval graders: no-skill-fired matches every qual skill; no-record cases also forbid .qual writes","supersedes":"251904038e9e3751ce1715023839206a26b69b043cd8809b6143cbea3d19efae","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
